    "body": "## Problem\r\n#41973 could not succeed due to failing tests\r\n## Solution\r\nFix failing tests, so that #41958 can be successfully merged to Neovim `release-0.12` branch. I was getting `vim.fn (nil value)`, so I just ripgrepped through test files and saw that `n.fn` could be used instead. Probably a difference in how the test harness runs on master vs release-0.12 (not familiar at all with that).\r\n\r\nRun the specific test file locally with `TEST_FILE=test/functional/autocmd/filetype_spec.lua make functionaltest` and it showed that both tests passed.\r\n\r\n`vimfn.gen.lua` file is missing compared to #41958. I thought it would get automatically generated. Should I do something about that on my end?",
    "closed_at": "2026-09-18T18:10:17Z",
